<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cornelis Gooyer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cornelis Gooyer was the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> commander of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritius">Mauritius</a>, sent by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> in 1638 to set up a permanent post at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-port">Grand Port</a> in the south-east of the island. With a small garrison he cut <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebony">ebony</a> for export and supplied passing ships, but the settlement struggled. He was replaced by Adriaan van der Stel in 1639.</p></div>
